  "deletedAt": null,
  "details": "I ran into this bug when I was doing open mic. I decided to plug my sm58 (microphone) into my computer instead of using my headset's built-in mic. As soon as I turned on my audio interface, the game's audio cut out, and it didn't pick up my mic. When I switched back to my headset mic, other players could hear me (I asked them to emote), but I still couldn't hear them (or anything else in the game for that matter). I had to restart the game in order to get the audio working again. \n\nI'm not sure what caused this, but this is my setup:\n\nWindows 10,\nHTC Vive,\nRazer ManO' War gaming headset\nScarlett Solo audio interface\n\nAlso, when I restarted the game, there was unbearable lag (talking 5 fps), but it seemed to disappear when I opened the SteamVR overlay, yet came back when I closed the overlay. I'm also not sure the cause of this, but my PC is definitely capable of running the software.",
